1
00:01:41,729 --> 00:01:49,020
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:51,900
[Episode 10]

3
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:57,759
Everyone.

4
00:01:57,950 --> 00:02:00,480
I have something very important
to announce.

5
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:02,680
Our school is about to hold

6
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:04,060
its 50th-anniversary celebration.

7
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:05,550
Every class has to put on a performance.

8
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:08,060
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

9
00:02:07,510 --> 00:02:08,150
Yes.

10
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:10,150
It's very important.

11
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,870
We must pass the school committee's
preliminary selection first.

12
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:14,800
There will be about 10 performances.

13
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,150
Classes will compete for the spots.

14
00:02:16,150 --> 00:02:18,030
But it's not mandatory.
It's completely voluntary.

15
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:18,750
All right?

16
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:19,430
Tang Tingting,

17
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:20,360
you organize this.

18
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,880
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

19
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,030
Okay.

20
00:02:21,630 --> 00:02:22,829
Take this seriously.

21
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,400
Everyone, everyone.

22
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:30,120
This is a great chance
to go down in school history.

23
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,150
What talents do you have?

24
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,400
Let me coordinate.

25
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:33,360
Me, me!

26
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:37,430
I have lots of talents.

27
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:39,710
Come on.

28
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:41,280
You've been tone-deaf
since you were a kid.

29
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,150
Just play basketball

30
00:02:42,150 --> 00:02:43,750
and be a good sports student.

31
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:46,680
Arts and sports go hand in hand.

32
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:49,240
Even if I, Duan Qiyan, don't say a word,

33
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,470
just standing there,

34
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:52,870
I am a beautiful sight.

35
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:56,750
Why the booing?

36
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:58,240
Am I not handsome?

37
00:02:58,690 --> 00:02:59,630
Duan Qiyan.

38
00:03:00,030 --> 00:03:01,840
Why don't you perform a sketch

39
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:04,120
called "Narcissism"?

40
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:05,630
Shoo!

41
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,150
Stop joking around, guys.

42
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:10,120
Be serious. This is important.

43
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:12,680
But hasn't the experimental class

44
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:14,740
always skipped these performances?

45
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,560
That's exactly why we should participate.

46
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,630
We should be
a different experimental class.

47
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:20,760
Who says we only know how to take tests?

48
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:24,800
Tingting, you're taking this so seriously.

49
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,750
Are you competing
with Zhao Shuran from Class 3

50
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:28,190
again?

51
00:03:28,470 --> 00:03:29,840
After all, you've been competing
since junior high

52
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,240
up until now.

53
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:35,520
No, I keep personal
and public matters separate, okay?

54
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,000
I really want our experimental class

55
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,400
to do well
in this kind of activity for once.

56
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:42,210
Who says good students
only know how to study?

57
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:44,560
W-With your grades?

58
00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:52,000
The 10th graders are quite active.

59
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,730
Every class has a performance.

60
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,030
This 50th-anniversary celebration

61
00:03:55,030 --> 00:03:57,280
is indeed a great chance to perform.

62
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,750
Miss, this is ours.

63
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:07,100
Tingting, what about your class?

64
00:04:11,590 --> 00:04:12,750
I...

65
00:04:13,030 --> 00:04:14,030
We...

66
00:04:14,910 --> 00:04:15,750
It's blank?

67
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:19,040
Don't tell me your class
doesn't have a single performance.

68
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:19,920
Makes sense.

69
00:04:20,310 --> 00:04:23,510
Your experimental class
just needs to focus on studying.

70
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:29,240
Who says we don't have one?

71
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:30,870
We have too many ideas

72
00:04:30,870 --> 00:04:32,150
we can't even choose.

73
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:33,800
Teacher.

74
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:35,240
We'll do an internal screening first.

75
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,480
Just look forward to it.

76
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,240
Sure.

77
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:48,430
What kind of performance should we do?

78
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:49,680
Help me think of something.

79
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:51,540
I really can't think of anything.

80
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,480
Even though you and Zhao Shuran

81
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:56,409
were bitter rivals in junior high,

82
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:58,120
we're already in high school now,

83
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,240
and you aren't in the same class.

84
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,370
Why is she still giving you a hard time?

85
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:05,630
Why are you two rivals?

86
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:09,330
It shouldn't be about grades, right?

87
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,630
How is that possible?

88
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:12,980
It's over their idols.

89
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:17,070
Really?
Fighting over people you don't know?

90
00:05:17,690 --> 00:05:19,610
No, no, no. There's more to it.

91
00:05:19,630 --> 00:05:20,450
Right.

92
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:22,060
Since school started,

93
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:24,060
they've been fighting
to lead the morning exercises

94
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:26,330
and the eye exercises.

95
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:28,300
Anyway...

96
00:05:29,010 --> 00:05:31,070
Zhao Shuran and Tingting are rivals.

97
00:05:35,130 --> 00:05:36,570
That's so interesting.

98
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:38,430
And looking at the situation now,

99
00:05:38,570 --> 00:05:40,630
it's no longer about personal honor.

100
00:05:40,659 --> 00:05:41,980
It is now

101
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:44,040
a battle to defend our class's honor.

102
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:47,390
Fight for the collective.

103
00:05:48,370 --> 00:05:49,430
Then I support you.

104
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:51,550
Spiritually.

105
00:05:56,010 --> 00:05:57,220
Let me remind you,

106
00:05:57,890 --> 00:06:00,570
tomorrow is the deadline for sign-ups.

107
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:04,660
I've already talked big,

108
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:06,720
so we have to put on a show this time...

109
00:06:07,250 --> 00:06:08,580
and blow everyone away!

110
00:06:10,690 --> 00:06:11,550
Arms wide open.

111
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:15,390
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

112
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:19,810
Two, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

113
00:06:21,330 --> 00:06:22,180
Look at them.

114
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:23,540
They are so in sync.

115
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,130
Looking at it this way,

116
00:06:25,130 --> 00:06:26,590
they're pretty cool, huh?

117
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:29,420
Five, six, seven, eight.

118
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:30,770
Two, two...

119
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:32,330
In sync?

120
00:06:33,330 --> 00:06:34,130
Cool?

121
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:36,470
Get ready to change direction.

122
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:41,270
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

123
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,570
A boy group dance?

124
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:02,770
The three of us?

125
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:09,710
Do you two know how to dance?

126
00:07:12,010 --> 00:07:13,620
Y-You do?

127
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:21,100
I've never even seen one before.

128
00:07:22,450 --> 00:07:23,250
Beautiful.

129
00:07:23,370 --> 00:07:24,700
It's really beautiful.

130
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:25,810
This is the trendiest

131
00:07:25,810 --> 00:07:27,340
formation dance right now.

132
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:29,330
It's easy to learn,
dance in sync, and is cool.

133
00:07:29,330 --> 00:07:30,980
When I saw you guys
warming up over there just now,

134
00:07:30,980 --> 00:07:31,770
you were so in sync.

135
00:07:31,770 --> 00:07:33,170
You can definitely do it.

136
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:34,060
Sis,

137
00:07:34,330 --> 00:07:35,130
our warm-up

138
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:36,990
is nothing like a boy group dance.

139
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:39,540
Please, guys.

140
00:07:39,770 --> 00:07:40,690
We absolutely cannot

141
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:42,659
let Zhao Shuran make a joke out of us.

142
00:07:42,659 --> 00:07:44,450
Right now, the most reliable option

143
00:07:44,450 --> 00:07:45,420
is you guys.

144
00:07:46,690 --> 00:07:48,370
If we really participate,

145
00:07:48,690 --> 00:07:50,500
that would be the biggest joke.

146
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:52,100
Just give it a try.

147
00:07:52,690 --> 00:07:54,620
Zhixia, please help me persuade them.

148
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,060
Please.

149
00:07:56,890 --> 00:07:58,300
J-J-J-J-Jiang Yubai.

150
00:08:15,570 --> 00:08:16,570
Why are you

151
00:08:16,810 --> 00:08:18,420
s-s-s-s-stuttering?

152
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:27,860
Well...

153
00:08:28,370 --> 00:08:30,740
Don't you still owe Lin Zhixia your life?

154
00:08:30,740 --> 00:08:32,409
This is a good chance to pay her back.

155
00:08:32,409 --> 00:08:33,100
What's going on?

156
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,700
That's a big change in attitude.

157
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:35,700
What's the trick?

158
00:08:36,169 --> 00:08:38,940
So what do you say?

159
00:08:40,370 --> 00:08:42,340
Did you agree?

160
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,460
Shen Fuxuan, what about you?

161
00:08:52,050 --> 00:08:53,340
With the both of them around,

162
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:55,170
I won't be the worst one.

163
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:55,980
Yes!

164
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:58,250
Now we're only short of two people
to complete the team.

165
00:08:58,250 --> 00:08:59,710
I'll go look around again.

166
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:09,620
Classmates,

167
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:13,010
since we signed up
for this school anniversary performance,

168
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:14,700
our experimental class

169
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:17,580
must beat
all the other performances in the school.

170
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:18,300
All right.

171
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:20,820
Now let me teach you how to dance.

172
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:24,400
[Dream OK]

173
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,510
♪ To me, say hi ♪

174
00:09:24,650 --> 00:09:25,410
Rub.

175
00:09:25,930 --> 00:09:27,380
♪ Open your heart quickly ♪

176
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:28,150
Open and close. Snap your fingers.

177
00:09:28,250 --> 00:09:28,860
Dust it off.

178
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,880
♪ To me, say hi ♪

179
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:30,220
Your shoes are dirty. Dust it off.

180
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,050
Twist.

181
00:09:30,490 --> 00:09:32,230
♪ We share the same dream ♪

182
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:36,810
♪ How lucky I am to have you
always by my side ♪

183
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:41,390
♪ Like a wave lifting a boat ♪

184
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:44,310
♪ Riding the wind to the sky ♪

185
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:04,220
Stop!

186
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:06,460
What's this you're dancing?

187
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:07,980
Your postures are terrible.

188
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:09,890
You'll never become
a boy group in your lifetime.

189
00:10:09,890 --> 00:10:11,740
Tang Tingting, just let us off the hook.

190
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:13,580
We haven't received
any professional training.

191
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,580
It's good enough
that we can remember the moves.

192
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:16,410
That's right.

193
00:10:16,910 --> 00:10:18,580
This is a formation dance.

194
00:10:18,890 --> 00:10:19,720
Formation moves

195
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,870
should be as neat as a full array.

196
00:10:21,940 --> 00:10:23,460
Not a single posture can be wrong.

197
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:25,370
You guys are dancing so messily.

198
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:25,890
If people didn't know,

199
00:10:25,890 --> 00:10:29,090
they would think
you were a group of scattered deserters.

200
00:10:32,610 --> 00:10:33,410
It's fine.

201
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:36,290
If this doesn't wory,

202
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:37,950
we can find another way.

203
00:10:43,010 --> 00:10:43,890
I

204
00:10:44,050 --> 00:10:47,170
once at the Cultural Festival of
the Normal University Affiliated Primary School,

205
00:10:47,170 --> 00:10:49,940
played a very important role,

206
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:52,530
and won the unanimous praise

207
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:55,170
of all the teachers and students
in the school.

208
00:10:55,170 --> 00:10:56,370
Shut up.

209
00:10:56,370 --> 00:10:58,940
That performance was called
"The Child on Horseback."

210
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:00,740
He played the horse in it.

211
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:02,050
He even used a cardboard

212
00:11:02,050 --> 00:11:03,370
to make a horse head
and put it on his head.

213
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:04,480
If the host hadn't said

214
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,370
that Duan Qiyan was in this performance,

215
00:11:05,370 --> 00:11:07,700
I wouldn't have realized
it was him at all.

216
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:09,600
You talk too much, Tang Tingting.

217
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:19,410
I'm exhausted.

218
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:21,620
Damn.

219
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:23,890
Don't go.

220
00:11:23,890 --> 00:11:24,650
Come.

221
00:11:30,820 --> 00:11:31,980
Their dancing

222
00:11:31,980 --> 00:11:34,220
is much better than ours.

223
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:36,410
Look at those

224
00:11:36,410 --> 00:11:37,070
dance moves

225
00:11:37,130 --> 00:11:38,130
and their

226
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:40,010
figures.

227
00:11:42,370 --> 00:11:43,740
Okay, pause at this move.

228
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:44,890
This is so beautiful.

229
00:11:44,890 --> 00:11:46,420
We can't compete with this.

230
00:11:47,770 --> 00:11:49,080
Which class is the one in the middle from?

231
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,050
Do you know her?

232
00:11:50,530 --> 00:11:51,890
-Please introduce her to me.
-Okay, everyone.

233
00:11:51,890 --> 00:11:53,550
Be serious. Let's do it again.

234
00:11:59,190 --> 00:12:00,580
I'm so mad.

235
00:12:01,170 --> 00:12:03,430
I absolutely cannot lose to Zhao Shuran.

236
00:12:04,410 --> 00:12:05,770
Stop looking. Let's go.

237
00:12:05,790 --> 00:12:06,840
Let's go.

238
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:08,010
Let's go.

239
00:12:11,770 --> 00:12:13,220
Two hours.

240
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:15,100
A whole two hours,

241
00:12:15,190 --> 00:12:16,860
and you still can't get
a single measure right.

242
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:18,700
Even a pig
would have learned it if I taught it.

243
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:20,760
You idiots who only know how to study!

244
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:26,520
The thought of losing to Zhao Shuran—

245
00:12:27,170 --> 00:12:29,290
and losing so terribly at it—

246
00:12:30,130 --> 00:12:32,250
makes me not want to go to school anymore.

247
00:12:32,250 --> 00:12:33,510
We have so many people.

248
00:12:33,770 --> 00:12:36,630
We are capable of thinking of
another performance.

249
00:12:38,170 --> 00:12:39,290
Lin Zhixia.

250
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:40,770
You're smart.

251
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:42,290
As our head planner,

252
00:12:42,290 --> 00:12:43,050
you have to help me

253
00:12:43,050 --> 00:12:44,620
put this show together.

254
00:12:55,010 --> 00:12:56,370
So, tell me everyone,

255
00:12:56,370 --> 00:12:57,530
what can you all do?

256
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:00,250
I know Jiang Yubai can play the piano.

257
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:01,710
What about the rest of you?

258
00:13:01,770 --> 00:13:03,380
Any other special talents?

259
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:05,250
I can play Go.

260
00:13:06,130 --> 00:13:07,820
You can't perform Go on stage.

261
00:13:08,410 --> 00:13:09,250
What else?

262
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:11,720
I can play the clapper.

263
00:13:14,290 --> 00:13:16,010
I can play the cello.

264
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:18,300
I can play the drums.

265
00:13:21,250 --> 00:13:23,250
So many of you can play instruments.

266
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,770
Let's form a band then!

267
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:37,130
A band?

268
00:13:37,170 --> 00:13:38,230
That's a good idea.

269
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:40,580
Jiang Yubai can be the keyboardist,

270
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,420
and Shen Fuxuan the drummer.

271
00:13:42,770 --> 00:13:44,100
I'll be the lead singer.

272
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:46,940
Then we're still missing...

273
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:50,100
The bass and cello

274
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:51,170
both have four strings.

275
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:52,290
The notes are the same.

276
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,290
I can give it a try.

277
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:54,530
Wait, no need.

278
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:56,860
You just stick to your cello.

279
00:13:57,410 --> 00:13:58,980
I can play the bass!

280
00:14:01,530 --> 00:14:03,330
Since when can you play the bass?

281
00:14:03,740 --> 00:14:05,740
I grew up with you.

282
00:14:05,890 --> 00:14:07,290
If you could really play the bass,

283
00:14:07,290 --> 00:14:08,740
with your love for bragging,

284
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:09,940
wouldn't you have told us
you've performed at

285
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:11,400
the Golden Hall in Vienna?

286
00:14:13,290 --> 00:14:15,940
I just didn't have a chance
to perform bass.

287
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:19,250
You can sing and play the guitar, right?

288
00:14:19,770 --> 00:14:21,620
You can sing and play the piano, right?

289
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:24,620
When have you ever seen someone
sing and play the bass?

290
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:26,650
Besides,

291
00:14:28,620 --> 00:14:29,740
I am a person

292
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:32,460
who is naturally modest and low-key.

293
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:36,460
All right, don't make a fuss.

294
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:37,820
In short,

295
00:14:38,130 --> 00:14:38,890
when the time comes,

296
00:14:38,890 --> 00:14:41,010
just see how well I do.

297
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:44,220
All right!

298
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:47,530
Then we are just short of a guitarist.

299
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:48,960
I'll take care of that.

300
00:14:49,290 --> 00:14:50,050
Great!

301
00:14:50,050 --> 00:14:51,580
We have a new performance then!

302
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:53,220
Our band will definitely

303
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:54,480
set the campus on fire!

304
00:15:19,650 --> 00:15:22,050
Is this guitarist you invited reliable?

305
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:24,000
Don't worry.

306
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,240
Absolutely reliable.

307
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,510
Although I haven't met him,

308
00:15:26,510 --> 00:15:28,820
he is the champion of the Hellfire Guitar

309
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:29,960
Solo Competition.

310
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,240
What's wrong?

311
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:36,870
What did you say?

312
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:40,820
The Hellfire Guitar Solo Competition.

313
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,170
The previous sentence.

314
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,650
Although I haven't met him.

315
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:53,370
We're internet friends.

316
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:56,130
It's normal that we haven't met.

317
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:01,650
By the way,

318
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:02,650
if he comes later,

319
00:16:02,650 --> 00:16:04,380
we still need to be a bit formal.

320
00:16:05,010 --> 00:16:06,980
Has our band not been named yet?

321
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:08,820
Let's name it now.

322
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,600
How about "Class Break"?

323
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,320
It gives the feeling

324
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,440
of using the precious 10-minute Class Break

325
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,570
in the midst of your busy and stressful

326
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:23,630
student life to do

327
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:24,960
what you like and love.

328
00:16:28,270 --> 00:16:29,270
That's a good one.

329
00:16:38,990 --> 00:16:40,840
Bro, your bass.

330
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:49,600
This bass is really nice.

331
00:16:58,870 --> 00:16:59,670
Boss,

332
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:04,270
which of these four strings is Do?

333
00:17:17,290 --> 00:17:18,010
Wind?

334
00:17:19,069 --> 00:17:19,960
Are you Wind?

335
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,920
Burst, reality.

336
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,720
Shatter, spirit.

337
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:33,070
Banish...

338
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:34,550
This world.

339
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,310
Angel's Tears?

340
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,300
How did you know it was me?

341
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:44,120
You dress exactly
like your QQ Show avatar.

342
00:17:57,550 --> 00:17:58,350
He's so cool.

343
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:01,310
He looks the part.

344
00:18:01,470 --> 00:18:02,870
Let's observe a bit more.

345
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,240
What would you like to drink?

346
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:08,900
No, thanks.

347
00:18:09,590 --> 00:18:10,790
Let's cut to the chase

348
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:12,120
and talk about music.

349
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:13,530
Okay.

350
00:18:14,030 --> 00:18:15,110
Our band's name

351
00:18:15,110 --> 00:18:15,920
is Class Break.

352
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:16,790
I'm the lead singer,

353
00:18:16,790 --> 00:18:17,880
and this is the keyboardist.

354
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:19,550
This is our band manager, Lin Zhixia.

355
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:21,610
Now, we're just missing a guitarist.

356
00:18:22,550 --> 00:18:24,110
What genre do you play?

357
00:18:24,690 --> 00:18:25,720
C-pop.

358
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:27,480
What's that?

359
00:18:53,350 --> 00:18:54,510
Thanks. Thanks.

360
00:18:56,110 --> 00:18:57,590
What genre do you like?

361
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,380
We are open to discussion.

362
00:19:00,370 --> 00:19:01,770
Open to discussion, huh?

363
00:19:02,230 --> 00:19:02,960
Okay.

364
00:19:04,370 --> 00:19:05,980
Then let me show you

365
00:19:06,740 --> 00:19:07,800
what real music is.

366
00:19:22,070 --> 00:19:24,880
Rock never dies!

367
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:32,920
I... I'm the guitarist.

368
00:19:33,270 --> 00:19:35,130
The lead singer isn't here, so...

369
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:38,660
Will this song do?

370
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,160
If we perform "Rock Never Dies"
at the school anniversary,

371
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:48,110
we'll die first.

372
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:49,400
Yeah.

373
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:51,440
Can we change to a song

374
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:53,030
that isn't so hardcore?

375
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:55,400
Not so hardcore means...

376
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:56,570
Pop rock?

377
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:00,030
Hey.

378
00:20:00,030 --> 00:20:02,350
I know it might be too simple for you,

379
00:20:02,350 --> 00:20:03,480
but pop rock

380
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:04,740
is already hard for us.

381
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:08,710
Here's the thing.

382
00:20:09,190 --> 00:20:11,240
I'm in the heavy metal scene.

383
00:20:11,430 --> 00:20:13,160
I don't play mainstream music.

384
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:14,850
If my peers knew

385
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,200
I performed pop songs at your school,

386
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:19,110
it would be embarrassing.

387
00:20:19,870 --> 00:20:20,630
Forget it.

388
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:21,720
Find someone else.

389
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:22,780
How about this?

390
00:20:23,510 --> 00:20:25,370
Just treat it as a commercial gig.

391
00:20:25,530 --> 00:20:27,570
We'll pay you 200.

392
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:30,080
200?

393
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:33,920
Outside,

394
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:36,400
my appearance fee is 600.

395
00:20:38,090 --> 00:20:39,290
I sing 8 songs a night.

396
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:41,950
Your 200...

397
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:44,120
Bro, with us,

398
00:20:44,140 --> 00:20:45,860
you get 200 for 1 song.

399
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:48,110
Outside, you average 75 a song.

400
00:20:51,350 --> 00:20:52,390
Is that so?

401
00:20:58,320 --> 00:21:00,520
You guys... you're doing 1 song, right?

402
00:21:02,790 --> 00:21:03,560
All right.

403
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:06,370
Find a good song

404
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:07,950
and send me the sheet music.

405
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:09,860
That's 200, okay?

406
00:21:27,790 --> 00:21:29,110
Why is there no sound?

407
00:21:32,430 --> 00:21:34,200
I'm playing it right.

408
00:21:44,350 --> 00:21:45,480
Duan Qiyan!

409
00:21:45,970 --> 00:21:46,970
I'm telling you,

410
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:48,240
if you play it again,

411
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:50,350
get out of here with your bass!

412
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,110
Dad!

413
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,400
Don't break my bass.

414
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,510
I rented it.

415
00:22:03,140 --> 00:22:04,030
Attention, everyone.

416
00:22:04,030 --> 00:22:06,400
This question
will definitely be in the exam.

417
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,810
As time goes by,

418
00:22:07,830 --> 00:22:09,030
the speed decreases.

419
00:22:09,110 --> 00:22:09,810
As we know,

420
00:22:09,810 --> 00:22:11,640
this is a downward deceleration of a.

421
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:13,000
Then for line d,

422
00:22:13,590 --> 00:22:14,550
let's analyze

423
00:22:14,790 --> 00:22:16,980
what its state is.

424
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:24,600
How is it going, Committee Member Tang?

425
00:22:24,790 --> 00:22:26,400
The performance of our class

426
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,500
is already very mature.

427
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:31,070
I'm considering whether to enrich

428
00:22:31,070 --> 00:22:32,310
the form of the dance.

429
00:22:32,470 --> 00:22:34,920
For instance,
adding poetry recitation to the dance.

430
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:36,450
Will it be more impressive?

431
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:39,070
Now my mind is full of

432
00:22:39,070 --> 00:22:40,510
these things every day.

433
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:42,100
It's giving me a headache.

434
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:45,580
I heard

435
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:46,720
your class's boy group dance

436
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:47,750
screwed up.

437
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:50,980
What new performance
are you preparing to change it to?

438
00:22:54,110 --> 00:22:56,550
Tang Tingting, I'm talking to you!

439
00:22:58,550 --> 00:22:59,720
So rude.

440
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:14,080
[Dance is the hidden language of the soul]

441
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:18,510
Stop.

442
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:19,590
Stop.

443
00:23:21,550 --> 00:23:22,610
We can't rehearse.

444
00:23:23,030 --> 00:23:23,790
What's wrong, bro?

445
00:23:23,790 --> 00:23:24,550
We can't.

446
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:28,160
The bass is terrible.

447
00:23:28,830 --> 00:23:31,090
The pitch is all wrong. Can't you hear it?

448
00:23:32,750 --> 00:23:34,200
Bro, teach me.

449
00:23:32,930 --> 00:23:34,580
[Dance is the hidden language of the soul]

450
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,110
I'll practice more.

451
00:23:35,110 --> 00:23:36,640
It's not about practicing.

452
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:37,680
In a band,

453
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:40,010
if the bass is a mess,
everything is a mess.

454
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:42,160
It's better not to have one, really.

455
00:23:48,350 --> 00:23:49,810
We can't do without a bass.

456
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:51,200
If the bass and the cello

457
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,200
are similar,

458
00:23:52,390 --> 00:23:53,480
I can give it a try.

459
00:24:00,390 --> 00:24:01,690
[Dance is the hidden language of the soul]

460
00:24:18,110 --> 00:24:19,200
That sounds okay.

461
00:24:19,570 --> 00:24:21,030
Here is someone who knows.

462
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:22,790
Let her play.

463
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:26,110
Bro, let me try again.

464
00:24:26,830 --> 00:24:27,920
Don't bother.

465
00:24:28,240 --> 00:24:29,830
You have no foundation.

466
00:24:29,830 --> 00:24:31,630
There is no time to train you now.

467
00:24:31,830 --> 00:24:32,790
Please teach me.

468
00:24:32,790 --> 00:24:33,920
I learn things quickly.

469
00:24:33,920 --> 00:24:34,750
Really.

470
00:24:34,750 --> 00:24:36,160
I only took 200 yuan.

471
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:37,480
Do I have to teach you for that as well?

472
00:24:37,480 --> 00:24:38,590
I'll pay you more.

473
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:40,720
It's not about the money. There's no need,

474
00:24:40,720 --> 00:24:41,440
you know?

475
00:24:42,070 --> 00:24:42,680
Bro,

476
00:24:42,880 --> 00:24:44,000
I really can't leave the band.

477
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:44,640
How about

478
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:46,070
you give me some other tasks?

479
00:24:46,070 --> 00:24:46,800
For example,

480
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:48,160
triangle, hourglass,

481
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:49,160
I can do anything.

482
00:24:49,750 --> 00:24:50,640
Forget it. Just don't

483
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:52,830
delay everyone's progress, okay?

484
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:57,590
Guys.

485
00:24:58,400 --> 00:24:59,330
Be softer today.

486
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:01,480
My throat isn't feeling well today.

487
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:04,110
Tingting.

488
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:05,830
You've been resting for a day.

489
00:25:05,830 --> 00:25:07,360
Why are you still like this?

490
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:08,810
I don't know either.

491
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:10,510
Can you still sing?

492
00:25:11,400 --> 00:25:12,270
I can't talk,

493
00:25:12,510 --> 00:25:14,040
but I can try singing again.

494
00:25:23,550 --> 00:25:26,820
♪ Running to the territory
I want to explore ♪

495
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:33,230
♪ Running to the territory
I want to explore ♪

496
00:25:33,350 --> 00:25:34,610
Stop, stop.

497
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:36,240
If you ask me,

498
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:37,740
let's just disband the band.

499
00:25:37,740 --> 00:25:38,220
Okay?

500
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:42,010
No, no.

501
00:25:42,110 --> 00:25:44,570
My voice will be fine
after a few days of rest.

502
00:25:46,720 --> 00:25:48,880
Actually, looking for an outsider

503
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,070
for your school anniversary

504
00:25:50,070 --> 00:25:51,750
is pretty unreal.

505
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,750
Forget it, I won't make this money.

506
00:25:54,750 --> 00:25:55,480
But...

507
00:25:55,510 --> 00:25:57,030
Feng, this program
is really important to us—

508
00:25:57,030 --> 00:25:58,050
super important—

509
00:25:58,080 --> 00:26:00,700
really important!

510
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:07,070
Jin Baihui?

511
00:26:09,110 --> 00:26:09,920
Excuse me.

512
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:12,440
Can I have a try?

513
00:26:14,480 --> 00:26:15,480
You can sing?

514
00:26:17,510 --> 00:26:19,110
I wrote a song myself.

515
00:26:19,110 --> 00:26:20,770
I don't know if it's suitable.

516
00:26:23,110 --> 00:26:24,640
You know how to write songs?

517
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:27,920
We want to listen.

518
00:26:39,290 --> 00:26:40,020
♪ Waiting ♪

519
00:26:40,940 --> 00:26:44,800
♪ Every second is patience ♪

520
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:46,320
♪ Run away quickly ♪

521
00:26:46,930 --> 00:26:50,400
♪ Testing with ulterior motives ♪

522
00:26:50,930 --> 00:26:52,370
♪ If I start over ♪

523
00:26:53,520 --> 00:26:57,240
♪ Why not now? ♪

524
00:26:57,810 --> 00:26:58,510
♪ It will turn around ♪

525
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:02,080
♪ Create accidents for accidents ♪

526
00:27:02,350 --> 00:27:03,030
It sounds good.

527
00:27:02,890 --> 00:27:05,250
♪ Break all fake love ♪

528
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:04,500
Sounds so good.

529
00:27:09,510 --> 00:27:11,110
Is this really a song you wrote?

530
00:27:11,110 --> 00:27:12,390
What's the name?

531
00:27:12,830 --> 00:27:14,760
This song is called "Closed Loop."

532
00:27:15,310 --> 00:27:16,000
This works.

533
00:27:25,030 --> 00:27:25,970
Great.

534
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,530
We have our own lead singer.

535
00:27:43,110 --> 00:27:43,980
[Let's build
a glorious campus dream together]

536
00:27:45,270 --> 00:27:47,070
Slow down. I can't understand.

537
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:50,950
I said our band is complete!

538
00:27:51,090 --> 00:27:52,460
Okay, stop talking.

539
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:53,830
Protect your voice.

540
00:27:56,210 --> 00:27:56,700
Wait, wait.

541
00:27:56,700 --> 00:27:57,160
Wait!

542
00:27:57,440 --> 00:27:58,070
Wait...

543
00:27:58,830 --> 00:28:00,030
You two wait a minute.

544
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:02,510
Since Wan Chunlei is playing the bass,

545
00:28:02,510 --> 00:28:03,440
what do I do?

546
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:07,960
Your mind is the one that's blank.

547
00:28:07,960 --> 00:28:08,880
I'm already on track.

548
00:28:08,880 --> 00:28:09,550
I don't need more—

549
00:28:09,550 --> 00:28:10,750
just give me a week.

550
00:28:10,750 --> 00:28:12,610
I promise I can practice until...

551
00:28:15,590 --> 00:28:16,270
Your head's going to explore?

552
00:28:16,270 --> 00:28:17,550
I should be the one saying that.

553
00:28:17,550 --> 00:28:19,350
I just ordered uniforms for our band.

554
00:28:19,350 --> 00:28:21,240
At least save a spot for me.

555
00:28:26,790 --> 00:28:28,960
Tang Tingting, I won't play a horse.

556
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:30,760
If you want to, play it yourself.

557
00:28:31,160 --> 00:28:32,560
You can understand this?

558
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:33,270
Well,

559
00:28:33,790 --> 00:28:35,480
you can't understand it?

560
00:28:35,750 --> 00:28:37,610
She was straight out scolding me.

561
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:50,100
We are all looking forward
to you playing the horse.

562
00:28:51,070 --> 00:28:52,750
I won't play the horse.

563
00:28:52,930 --> 00:28:54,000
How old am I?

564
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,330
Playing a horse for fun?

565
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:57,070
Zhixia, no need to persuade me.

566
00:28:57,070 --> 00:28:58,070
It's impossible.

567
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,600
Absolutely impossible!

568
00:29:11,460 --> 00:29:14,530
♪ The world is limitless colour puzzle ♪

569
00:29:14,780 --> 00:29:18,010
♪ I have the wildest dreams;
never fitting in ♪

570
00:29:18,370 --> 00:29:21,350
♪ The formula in my mind
is messed up and reorganized ♪

571
00:29:21,850 --> 00:29:24,940
♪ Is loneliness my only talent? ♪

572
00:29:25,610 --> 00:29:29,280
♪ Hide in the midsummer tree shade;
what's waiting for my answer? ♪

573
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:31,710
♪ The breeze blows past my cheeks ♪

574
00:29:32,530 --> 00:29:35,300
♪ How do I solve for
the unexpected variables? ♪

575
00:29:35,770 --> 00:29:38,550
♪ At the most splendid moment ♪

576
00:29:39,220 --> 00:29:42,340
♪ Running and waiting for my exploration ♪

577
00:29:42,620 --> 00:29:45,580
♪ The unknown is so fascinating ♪

578
00:29:46,100 --> 00:29:48,270
♪ Young me stood on tiptoes ♪

579
00:29:48,740 --> 00:29:52,720
♪ Everything is transparent;
time is too light ♪

580
00:29:53,060 --> 00:29:56,210
♪ Natural deduction;
the answer is clear in an instant ♪

581
00:29:56,440 --> 00:29:59,390
♪ The timer is still counting down
3, 2, 1 ♪

582
00:29:59,660 --> 00:30:02,140
♪ The best answer is within our reach ♪

583
00:30:02,470 --> 00:30:05,100
♪ How should I define ♪

584
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:06,320
♪ You and me ♪

585
00:30:06,820 --> 00:30:09,820
♪ Look up at my dream; so blue ♪

586
00:30:10,360 --> 00:30:11,670
♪ There are countless tests ♪

587
00:30:10,800 --> 00:30:14,520
[Class Break]

588
00:30:12,150 --> 00:30:13,670
♪ Different answers ♪

589
00:30:14,750 --> 00:30:16,830
♪ Life doesn't only have regrets ♪

590
00:30:16,560 --> 00:30:18,530
[Class Break]

591
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:22,390
♪ What shines brightly about us
is our courage ♪

592
00:30:47,700 --> 00:30:50,540
[Let's celebrate the school anniversary
of Nanhai No. 1 High School]

593
00:31:07,110 --> 00:31:07,790
What?

594
00:31:09,230 --> 00:31:10,350
How could this be?

595
00:31:13,180 --> 00:31:13,980
What's wrong?

596
00:31:15,510 --> 00:31:16,830
Wind said he's not coming.

597
00:31:16,830 --> 00:31:17,890
Wind's not coming.

598
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:19,070
He's going to

599
00:31:19,070 --> 00:31:20,590
an indie music festival.

600
00:31:20,720 --> 00:31:21,880
He's going to play real rock.

601
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:23,540
He's leaving this afternoon.

602
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:24,880
When will he be back?

603
00:31:24,880 --> 00:31:26,210
He said he doesn't know.

604
00:31:28,880 --> 00:31:30,440
A band without a guitarist—

605
00:31:30,440 --> 00:31:31,880
what kind of band is that?

606
00:31:39,070 --> 00:31:41,200
I wonder if I can fill in.

607
00:31:42,350 --> 00:31:45,150
You're just a cardboard horse
for entertainment.

608
00:31:45,350 --> 00:31:46,070
Do you know

609
00:31:46,070 --> 00:31:47,750
how important Wind is to us?

610
00:31:49,030 --> 00:31:51,640
He's the only professional among us.

611
00:31:52,440 --> 00:31:55,440
But it's too late for us
to change the performance now.

612
00:31:55,810 --> 00:31:57,210
I learn things very fast.

613
00:31:57,440 --> 00:31:58,910
I can skip sleep just to practice.

614
00:31:58,910 --> 00:32:00,570
And I've learned the bass before.

615
00:32:00,570 --> 00:32:02,500
I have some basic music knowledge.

616
00:32:03,350 --> 00:32:05,350
Although these two instruments look alike,

617
00:32:05,350 --> 00:32:08,010
they are different
when you actually play them.

618
00:32:09,590 --> 00:32:12,880
All our days of rehearsal will be wasted.

619
00:32:15,200 --> 00:32:17,730
Can you stop shouting
with that broken voice?

620
00:32:17,790 --> 00:32:19,050
Can't you trust me for once?

621
00:32:19,050 --> 00:32:20,050
At least let me...

622
00:32:20,070 --> 00:32:21,160
Let me try.

623
00:32:28,200 --> 00:32:29,930
There's no other way right now.

624
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:32,800
We can let Duan Qiyan try.

625
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:43,750
Duan Qiyan,

626
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:47,260
you must be prepared to endure hardship.

627
00:32:48,830 --> 00:32:49,680
Yes!

628
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:50,830
Zhixia,

629
00:32:51,030 --> 00:32:52,560
I owe you my life twice over.

630
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:56,110
Sir.

631
00:32:57,810 --> 00:32:59,270
Returning it so soon?

632
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:01,590
Your lease isn't up yet.

633
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:05,880
I can't get used to playing the bass.

634
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:07,610
I'll switch back to the guitar.

635
00:33:08,510 --> 00:33:09,120
Okay.

636
00:33:11,210 --> 00:33:12,460
Here, take this.

637
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:20,530
Sir,

638
00:33:22,350 --> 00:33:24,000
where is "Do" on this guitar?

639
00:33:26,020 --> 00:33:29,250
[Lead Guitar Licks]

640
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:32,720
Duan, let's go.

641
00:33:32,750 --> 00:33:33,920
Let's go play basketball.

642
00:33:33,920 --> 00:33:35,850
How can I play with my injured hand?

643
00:33:37,440 --> 00:33:38,550
Didn't you say that

644
00:33:38,640 --> 00:33:39,830
a hand injury is nothing,

645
00:33:39,830 --> 00:33:41,400
and you wouldn't complain
even if covered in bruises?

646
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:42,640
Is that the same?

647
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:44,160
Go ahead. Leave me alone.

648
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:44,960
I'm leaving.

649
00:33:48,030 --> 00:33:49,110
Really?

650
00:33:49,680 --> 00:33:51,280
Why haven't I heard about it?

651
00:33:59,790 --> 00:34:02,250
How did Duan Qiyan's fingers
get so worn out?

652
00:34:03,350 --> 00:34:04,400
Learning an instrument

653
00:34:04,400 --> 00:34:05,880
requires hard work.

654
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:07,640
The guitar relies mainly on the fingers

655
00:34:07,640 --> 00:34:09,969
rubbing against the strings repeatedly.

656
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:12,550
Just like working out builds muscle,

657
00:34:13,030 --> 00:34:14,360
to play the guitar well,

658
00:34:14,510 --> 00:34:17,370
you have to build up calluses
on your fingers first.

659
00:34:18,230 --> 00:34:20,560
You've played the piano, so you must know.

660
00:34:22,800 --> 00:34:24,070
But if this continues,

661
00:34:24,070 --> 00:34:26,550
he definitely won't be able
to perform on stage.

662
00:34:26,550 --> 00:34:29,010
We need to find a way
for him to learn quickly.

663
00:34:30,230 --> 00:34:32,880
Can there be any shortcuts to this?

664
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:35,360
You know music.

665
00:34:35,440 --> 00:34:36,880
Teach me after school.

666
00:34:50,320 --> 00:34:51,449
Sounds good, right?

667
00:34:52,190 --> 00:34:53,050
It sounds good.

668
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:55,230
But you can actually try

669
00:34:55,230 --> 00:34:56,670
playing with all 5 fingers together,

670
00:34:56,670 --> 00:34:58,200
and keep your hands lifted.

671
00:35:04,710 --> 00:35:06,110
How do I keep them lifted?

672
00:35:08,590 --> 00:35:09,150
Just...

673
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:10,340
I'll teach you.

674
00:35:10,960 --> 00:35:12,510
Right, lift it up a bit.

675
00:35:12,630 --> 00:35:13,510
Lift it up.

676
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:14,550
Then,

677
00:35:14,550 --> 00:35:16,350
right, use every finger to play.

678
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:17,230
Right.

679
00:35:17,930 --> 00:35:18,860
A little higher.

680
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:04,440
What about the left hand?

681
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:05,900
How should I place my left hand?

682
00:36:05,900 --> 00:36:07,760
I-It's the same for the left hand.

683
00:36:08,070 --> 00:36:09,630
Just... rest it here,

684
00:36:09,630 --> 00:36:10,890
and lift it up a little.

685
00:36:23,110 --> 00:36:24,710
Is it the same for the guitar?

686
00:36:26,920 --> 00:36:28,110
Not quite.

687
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:31,530
But piano and guitar
are actually quite similar.

688
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:33,150
Look,

689
00:36:33,510 --> 00:36:34,800
the C chord on a piano

690
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,960
is playing Do, Mi, Sol together.

691
00:36:39,070 --> 00:36:41,110
The C chord on a guitar
is also Do, Mi, Sol.

692
00:36:41,110 --> 00:36:42,190
It's just that on a piano,

693
00:36:42,190 --> 00:36:43,510
you press the keys,

694
00:36:43,510 --> 00:36:45,110
while on a guitar, you strum.

695
00:36:55,710 --> 00:36:57,400
Is it possible

696
00:36:57,630 --> 00:36:58,840
that there is something

697
00:36:58,840 --> 00:37:00,840
that can play a chord with one press?

698
00:37:04,360 --> 00:37:05,800
How would you

699
00:37:06,550 --> 00:37:08,010
make this one-press chord

700
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:09,510
work?

701
00:37:10,920 --> 00:37:12,650
I haven't figured that out yet.

702
00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:14,920
I just feel there must be a device

703
00:37:14,920 --> 00:37:16,320
that can replace fingers

704
00:37:16,630 --> 00:37:18,360
and play a chord with one press.

705
00:37:22,330 --> 00:37:24,680
I think we can give it a try.

706
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:52,460
♪ Wandering light wind
drifts past your pupils ♪

707
00:37:53,620 --> 00:37:57,940
♪ One second of encounter,
heartstrings stirred ♪

708
00:37:58,470 --> 00:38:01,830
♪ The story feels altogether different ♪

709
00:38:04,040 --> 00:38:11,780
♪ How to describe
my whimsical wandering dream? ♪

710
00:38:13,030 --> 00:38:17,250
♪ You softly answer my quirky side ♪

711
00:38:17,640 --> 00:38:20,980
♪ Such bliss to finally be understood ♪

712
00:38:21,170 --> 00:38:23,090
Through repeated attempts,

713
00:38:22,450 --> 00:38:26,790
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world came alive with color ♪

714
00:38:23,940 --> 00:38:24,940
Jiang Yubai and I

715
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:27,460
actually made a one-press chord device.

716
00:38:27,460 --> 00:38:31,830
♪ Could this be how love begins? ♪

717
00:38:29,420 --> 00:38:30,440
At that time,

718
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:32,980
we just thought it was a temporary fix.

719
00:38:32,350 --> 00:38:35,330
♪ These unspoken feelings
are so hard to figure out ♪

720
00:38:35,500 --> 00:38:36,960
But years later, I finally understood.

721
00:38:35,910 --> 00:38:41,230
♪ Hidden deep within your gaze ♪

722
00:38:37,940 --> 00:38:39,010
True rock and roll

723
00:38:39,590 --> 00:38:41,520
is never about perfect technique,

724
00:38:41,630 --> 00:38:46,020
♪ Sometimes, I imagine
drifting beyond the skies with you ♪

725
00:38:42,230 --> 00:38:43,480
but the passion of a group of people

726
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:45,190
who forge ahead

727
00:38:45,570 --> 00:38:47,550
through messy trials.

728
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:50,830
♪ Shimmering light
dances over the flower in bloom ♪

729
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:50,150
Now,

730
00:38:50,150 --> 00:38:51,920
there are more ways to learn the guitar.

731
00:38:51,310 --> 00:38:54,450
♪ After all we've been through,
our fates remain intertwined ♪

732
00:38:53,590 --> 00:38:55,690
But I miss the times
during the school anniversary so much.

733
00:38:55,200 --> 00:39:01,630
♪ Perhaps fate favors me now ♪

734
00:38:57,300 --> 00:38:59,840
Those youthful days

735
00:39:00,570 --> 00:39:02,670
that could be ignited with one press...
